# TypeScript & Fastify

- Use Zod for all request/response validation; attach schemas to routes with `fastify-type-provider-zod`.
- Handlers: thin layer – call service, then `reply.send()`. Put logic in `service.ts`.
- Use `FastifyError` with `statusCode` when throwing so the global error handler returns correct status.
- Type protected handlers with `AuthenticatedRequest` from `src/middleware/auth.ts` when using `authenticate` or `optionalAuth`.
- Prefer Drizzle in services; schema lives only in `src/db/schema.ts`.
